{"id":"n5_u04_l1","unit_id":"n5_u04","instructional_level":"N5","title":"Katakana I: vowels, K and S","goal":"Read katakana a, i, u, e, o and the k and s rows. Katakana is used for words borrowed from other languages.","introduces":{"kana":["ka_k_a","ka_k_i","ka_k_u","ka_k_e","ka_k_o","ka_k_ka","ka_k_ki","ka_k_ku","ka_k_ke","ka_k_ko","ka_k_sa","ka_k_shi","ka_k_su","ka_k_se","ka_k_so"],"vocab":["v_kokoa","v_aisu"]},"explain":[{"heading":"A second kana set","body":["Katakana has the same sounds as hiragana but different shapes: ア = あ, カ = か. It is used for foreign loanwords, names of foreign places and people, and emphasis.","Look-alikes to watch: シ (shi) and ツ (tsu) have almost-upright versus almost-flat short strokes; ソ and ン differ by the direction of the long stroke."],"examples":[{"ja":"ココア","reading":"kokoa","en":"cocoa"},{"ja":"アイス","reading":"aisu","en":"ice cream"}]}],"practice":{"question_ids":["q_n5u04_kr01","q_n5u04_kr02","q_n5u04_kr03","q_n5u04_kr04","q_n5u04_kr05","q_n5u04_kr07","q_n5u04_kr13","q_n5u04_kr20","q_n5u04_mt01","q_n5u04_mt02","q_n5u04_rc01","q_n5u04_rc02","q_n5u04_rc03","q_n5u04_rc04","q_n5u04_rc05","q_n5u04_rd01","q_n5u04_rd02","q_n5u04_vm_kokoa","q_n5u04_vm_aisu"],"gen":[{"type":"kana_recog","from":"kana","ids":["ka_k_a","ka_k_i","ka_k_u","ka_k_e","ka_k_o","ka_k_ka","ka_k_ki","ka_k_ku","ka_k_ke","ka_k_ko","ka_k_sa","ka_k_shi","ka_k_su","ka_k_se","ka_k_so"],"n":6},{"type":"kana_listen","from":"kana","ids":["ka_k_a","ka_k_i","ka_k_u","ka_k_e","ka_k_o","ka_k_ka","ka_k_ki","ka_k_ku","ka_k_ke","ka_k_ko","ka_k_sa","ka_k_shi","ka_k_su","ka_k_se","ka_k_so"],"n":4}]},"exit_check":{"gen":[{"type":"kana_recog","from":"kana","ids":["ka_k_a","ka_k_i","ka_k_u","ka_k_e","ka_k_o","ka_k_ka","ka_k_ki","ka_k_ku","ka_k_ke","ka_k_ko","ka_k_sa","ka_k_shi","ka_k_su","ka_k_se","ka_k_so"],"n":8}],"pass":0.7},"provenance":"orig"},
{"id":"n5_u04_l2","unit_id":"n5_u04","instructional_level":"N5","title":"Katakana II: T, N and H","goal":"Read the t, n and h rows of katakana and your first loanwords.","introduces":{"kana":["ka_k_ta","ka_k_chi","ka_k_tsu","ka_k_te","ka_k_to","ka_k_na","ka_k_ni","ka_k_nu","ka_k_ne","ka_k_no","ka_k_ha","ka_k_hi","ka_k_fu","ka_k_he","ka_k_ho"],"vocab":["v_tenisu","v_naifu","v_hamu","v_tomato","v_nekutai"]},"explain":[{"heading":"Three more rows","body":["タ チ ツ テ ト, ナ ニ ヌ ネ ノ, ハ ヒ フ ヘ ホ. Note ス (su) versus ヌ (nu): ヌ has an extra short stroke.","The sounds are the same as the hiragana rows: チ is \"chi\", ツ is \"tsu\", フ is \"fu\"."],"examples":[{"ja":"テニス","reading":"tenisu","en":"tennis"},{"ja":"トマト","reading":"tomato","en":"tomato"},{"ja":"ネクタイ","reading":"nekutai","en":"necktie"}]}],"practice":{"question_ids":["q_n5u04_kr06","q_n5u04_kr09","q_n5u04_kr10","q_n5u04_kr11","q_n5u04_kr12","q_n5u04_kr14","q_n5u04_kr15","q_n5u04_mt03","q_n5u04_mt04","q_n5u04_mt05","q_n5u04_rc06","q_n5u04_rc07","q_n5u04_rc08","q_n5u04_rc09","q_n5u04_rc10","q_n5u04_rc11","q_n5u04_rd03","q_n5u04_vm_tenisu","q_n5u04_vm_naifu","q_n5u04_vm_hamu","q_n5u04_vm_tomato","q_n5u04_vm_nekutai"],"gen":[{"type":"kana_recog","from":"kana","ids":["ka_k_ta","ka_k_chi","ka_k_tsu","ka_k_te","ka_k_to","ka_k_na","ka_k_ni","ka_k_nu","ka_k_ne","ka_k_no","ka_k_ha","ka_k_hi","ka_k_fu","ka_k_he","ka_k_ho"],"n":6},{"type":"kana_recall","from":"kana","ids":["ka_k_ta","ka_k_chi","ka_k_tsu","ka_k_te","ka_k_to","ka_k_na","ka_k_ni","ka_k_nu","ka_k_ne","ka_k_no","ka_k_ha","ka_k_hi","ka_k_fu","ka_k_he","ka_k_ho"],"n":4}]},"exit_check":{"gen":[{"type":"kana_recog","from":"kana","ids":["ka_k_a","ka_k_i","ka_k_u","ka_k_e","ka_k_o","ka_k_ka","ka_k_ki","ka_k_ku","ka_k_ke","ka_k_ko","ka_k_sa","ka_k_shi","ka_k_su","ka_k_se","ka_k_so","ka_k_ta","ka_k_chi","ka_k_tsu","ka_k_te","ka_k_to","ka_k_na","ka_k_ni","ka_k_nu","ka_k_ne","ka_k_no","ka_k_ha","ka_k_hi","ka_k_fu","ka_k_he","ka_k_ho"],"n":8}],"pass":0.7},"provenance":"orig"},
{"id":"n5_u04_l3","unit_id":"n5_u04","instructional_level":"N5","title":"Katakana III: M, Y, R, W and ン","goal":"Finish the basic katakana chart and read travel and food loanwords.","introduces":{"kana":["ka_k_ma","ka_k_mi","ka_k_mu","ka_k_me","ka_k_mo","ka_k_ya","ka_k_yu","ka_k_yo","ka_k_ra","ka_k_ri","ka_k_ru","ka_k_re","ka_k_ro","ka_k_wa","ka_k_wo","ka_k_n"],"vocab":["v_hoteru","v_kamera","v_miruku","v_meron","v_taoru","v_masuku","v_resutoran","v_amerika","v_roshia","v_sumaho","v_itaria","v_furansu","v_remon","v_wain","v_anime"]},"explain":[{"heading":"The last rows","body":["マ ミ ム メ モ, ヤ ユ ヨ, ラ リ ル レ ロ, ワ ヲ, ン. Compare ウ (u) with ワ (wa): ウ has a small mark on top.","ヲ is the katakana for \"o\" but is hardly ever used; you will rarely see it."],"examples":[{"ja":"ホテル","reading":"hoteru","en":"hotel"},{"ja":"カメラ","reading":"kamera","en":"camera"},{"ja":"アメリカ","reading":"amerika","en":"the United States"},{"ja":"レストラン","reading":"resutoran","en":"restaurant"}]}],"practice":{"question_ids":["q_n5u04_kr08","q_n5u04_kr16","q_n5u04_kr17","q_n5u04_kr18","q_n5u04_kr19","q_n5u04_mt06","q_n5u04_mt07","q_n5u04_mt08","q_n5u04_lk01","q_n5u04_lk02","q_n5u04_lk03","q_n5u04_lk04","q_n5u04_lk05","q_n5u04_lk06","q_n5u04_rc12","q_n5u04_rc13","q_n5u04_rc14","q_n5u04_rc15","q_n5u04_rc16","q_n5u04_rc17","q_n5u04_rc18","q_n5u04_rc19","q_n5u04_rc20","q_n5u04_rd04","q_n5u04_rd05","q_n5u04_rd06","q_n5u04_rd07","q_n5u04_rd08","q_n5u04_rd09","q_n5u04_rd10","q_n5u04_rd11","q_n5u04_rd12","q_n5u04_vm_hoteru","q_n5u04_vm_kamera","q_n5u04_vm_miruku","q_n5u04_vm_meron","q_n5u04_vm_taoru","q_n5u04_vm_masuku","q_n5u04_vm_resutoran","q_n5u04_vm_amerika","q_n5u04_vm_roshia","q_n5u04_vm_sumaho","q_n5u04_vm_itaria","q_n5u04_vm_furansu","q_n5u04_vm_remon","q_n5u04_vm_wain","q_n5u04_vm_anime"],"gen":[{"type":"kana_recog","from":"kana","ids":["ka_k_ma","ka_k_mi","ka_k_mu","ka_k_me","ka_k_mo","ka_k_ya","ka_k_yu","ka_k_yo","ka_k_ra","ka_k_ri","ka_k_ru","ka_k_re","ka_k_ro","ka_k_wa","ka_k_wo","ka_k_n"],"n":6